{"name":"Thundercloud","hex":"#698589","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thundercloud","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, dark cloud, usually a cumulonimbus, charged with electricity and producing thunder and lightning.","Something menacing and brooding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thundercloud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cumulonimbus cloud","blocks":[{"text":"Cumulonimbus is a dense, towering, vertical cloud types, typically forming from water vapor condensing in the lower troposphere that builds upward carried by powerful buoyant air currents. Above the lower portions of the cumulonimbus the water vapor becomes ice crystals, such as snow and graupel, the interaction of which can lead to hail and to lightning formation, respectively."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Cumulonimbus_incus_over_Warsaw%2C_Poland.jpg/330px-Cumulonimbus_incus_over_Warsaw%2C_Poland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumulonimbus_cloud","wikidata":"Q182311"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Large_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg/500px-Large_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Large_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg/1280px-Large_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Large_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg/500px-Large_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cumulonimbus calvus over El Bajío, Guanajuato, Mexico.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarge_cloud_over_Mexican_landscape.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t